think Last lap shipped image/compose_tiled.rye (paint_tiled) -- the CSS background-repeat gesture, tiling a pattern edge to edge. compose_tiled and compose both start a source at the box corner. The missing sibling is background-position with no-repeat: place ONE copy at a named anchor (start/center/end on each axis), the box's remaining area left as ground. A real surface need -- an icon pinned top-right, a logo centered in a card, a badge in a corner.
think Design: paint_placed(target,x,y,w,h,source,ax,ay). The crux is one axis rule seen twice (axis_window), all unsigned so no signed math: when the source FITS the box (src<=box) the whole source draws at an anchored offset (start 0, center on the slack/2, end on the slack); when it OVERFLOWS (src>box) a box-sized window of the source draws from the box corner, the anchor choosing src_off (start 0, center over/2, end over). Both cases keep every offset non-negative -- the reason to split fit vs overflow rather than reach for i64.
think Compose not braid held: compose.paint_over_region OWNS the blit, qoi owns both buffers; this rung only ROUTES the anchor to its one window and its one clip -- no new blend math, no new codec, no new color, not even a new pixel loop. The oversize-source clip reuses the exact same paint_over_region window mechanism compose_tiled uses for a boundary tile.
think Council rota lap deep-read foundations/20260703-182612_sameness-is-the-macro.md -- compress the system by public similarity, one value model, one vocabulary, so learning one part is learning many. Applied literally: place_paint is compose_tiled's sibling by SHAPE -- the same make_canvas/pixel_at/set_pixel/make_source helpers, the same up-front u64 bound check, the same all-or-nothing refusal grammar, the same selftest arc (seat, clip, blend, round-trip, refuse, determinism). A reader who knows compose_tiled reads place_paint for free.
obs Selftest GREEN on the first build; one witness red closed same-sitting -- the printed GREEN line carried "source's", and the witness grep guard wraps the line in single quotes, so the apostrophe closed the shell string and the grep missed. Reworded apostrophe-free ("the middle window of the source"). This is the SAME red the conic_paint lap hit (20260817.150028) -- a lantern that has now fired twice on the apostrophe-in-printed-line. Worth a loom: the witnesses could grep a file rather than an inlined single-quoted string, or the ASCII-first sweep could flag an apostrophe in a print line. Named here, not yet built -- narrow scope this lap.
obs The nine CSS background-position keywords fall out of one enum (Anchor: start/center/end) on two axes -- the "sameness is the macro" economy made literal, nine placements from one axis rule.
